---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="MCP client install matrix & skill paths | rea.run"
  description="Which coding agents REA setup supports, skill directory pitfalls, and doctor checks."
  path="/docs/mcp-clients/"
>
  <article class="prose-page mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14">
    <p class="text-sm"><a class="quiet-link" href="/faq/">← FAQ hub</a></p>

    <p class="badge badge-accent mt-4">Docs</p>
    <h1 class="display mt-4 text-4xl text-[var(--color-ink)]">MCP client install matrix &amp; skill paths</h1>
    <p class="lede mt-4 !max-w-none">Get REA registered with your coding agent — and make sure investigation skills land where the client actually loads them.</p>

    <h2>Setup in one line</h2>
    <p>Most hosts should use the package runner so the version matches what you expect:</p>
    <pre><code>npx -y rea-agents@6.4.0 setup</code></pre>
    <p>Review the plan, approve changes, then <strong>restart or reconnect</strong> the client. README / FAQ debt notes that docs sometimes say <code>rea setup</code> after a global install — both shapes exist; pin a version when you need reproducibility.</p>

    <h2>Client IDs live on the matrix page</h2>
    <p>
      <code>rea-agents@6.4.0</code> setup accepts 17 <code>--client</code> values, including Pi (<code>pi</code>), Hermes (<code>hermes</code>), Qwen Code (<code>qwen_code</code>), and GitHub Copilot CLI (<code>copilot_cli</code>).
      The full table, config paths, and the note that Factory Droid and <code>dsh</code> are pending the next npm release after 6.4.0 are on <a href="/docs/clients/">the client matrix</a>.
      Confirm a registration with <code>npx -y rea-agents@6.4.0 doctor --client … --json</code>.
    </p>
    <h2>Skill path pitfall</h2>
    <p>Setup may write an investigation skill to a directory the <em>package</em> considers canonical (for example under <code>~/.agents/skills</code>), while a specific client only auto-loads skills from its own tree (for example Claude Code reading <code>~/.claude/skills</code>). Symptom: MCP tools appear, but the agent never picks up REA’s workflow instructions.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>After setup, confirm where the skill file was written.</li>
      <li>If the client ignores that path, copy or symlink into the client’s skills directory — or re-run setup after upgrading past fixes that align discovery.</li>
      <li>Third-party skill installers (for example skills.sh-style flows) may install <strong>instructions only</strong> and <strong>do not</strong> register the MCP server. You still need MCP registration via setup or manual JSON.</li>
    </ul>
    <pre><code>npx -y rea-agents@6.4.0 doctor --client claude_code --json
npx -y rea-agents@6.4.0 doctor --skill --json</code></pre>

    <h2>Manual MCP shape</h2>
    <pre><code>{`{
  "mcpServers": {
    "rea": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "rea-agents@6.4.0", "mcp"]
    }
  }
}`}</code></pre>
    <p>Pin <code>rea-agents@VERSION</code> for lockstep environments.</p>

    <footer class="mt-12 border-t border-[var(--color-line)] pt-6 text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] not-prose">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider">Sources</p>
      <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5 text-xs">
          <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/issues/1337" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Issue #1337 — skill install path vs Claude Code load path</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/issues/1459" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Issue #1459 — skill discoverability</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/issues/1353" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Issue #1353 — setup command FAQ / docs</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/main/docs/installation.md" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Upstream installation docs</a></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-4"><a class="quiet-link" href="/compliance/">Compliance</a></p>
